# Virtual environment
.venv/
venv/
env/

# Python bytecode
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class

# Tool caches
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/

# Coverage reports
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Packaging artifacts
*.egg-info/
dist/
build/

# Editor and OS junk
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Project outputs (results, logs, saved runs)
results/
*.parquet
*.log


/////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////////
.venv/, venv/, env/ — three common names for the same thing. Costs nothing to cover all three.

.vscode/ is a judgement call. It holds your editor settings, which are personal, so most people exclude it. Some projects commit it deliberately to share a team config. Exclude it.

results/, *.parquet, *.log — nothing yet, but on day 19 your tournament will write large output files. Better to have the rule already in place than to accidentally push a 200 MB results file.

Thumbs.db is Windows' image thumbnail cache. .DS_Store is the macOS equivalent. Both harmless, both clutter every diff.